From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] brcmfmac: pcie: BCM4360 test.317 no side-writes fire #11

Fire #10 (0016) gave three results: (1) R3b -- ZERO NVRAM (replica of kimptoc's
test.28 substrate: no vars, no token at TCM[ramsize-4], varsz=0) -- console
wr_idx STILL 0x27d=637: NVRAM (content and presence) is excluded as cause
and lever; (2) P1-T -- SB intstatus=0x300 measured PRE-release, right after
the PLAIN write MAILBOXINT:=0xFFFFFFFF (masked to 0x3):
0x300 at kimptoc = mirror HW of his OWN pre-release write (his 'release' did
not clear the mailbox, so it survived; our chip_set_active clears it), NOT a
fw-side latch -- the "0x300 = fw sign of life" theory is DEFINITIVELY dead;
(3) console TAIL (25x read_ram32 @0x97194) -- a new class: kernel printk died
exactly on the "...TAIL ... now" line on a live machine (8/8 CPU, sysrq-511
zero lines, no AER/stuck task; insmod returned, module bound, T309 not
reached).

After fire #10 ONE untested difference vs kimptoc's test.28 remains: our
side-writes (T276 shared_info + olmsg ring + MAILBOXMASK RMW |=0x100 in
request_irq + H2D doorbell preinit dcmd) + pci_set_master (kimptoc ran with
BM-off). Patch 0017 does the MAXIMAL test.28 replication in one fire (test.317)
-- after release the host does ZERO writes:

a) bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo: skips the WHOLE test.276 pre-release write --
   no dma_alloc of the 64 KB olmsg ring, no ring header writes, no zeroing
   of the shared_info TCM region, no magic/dma_lo/dma_hi/buf_size/varsz/
   vars16/fw_init_done/magic_end. The substrate = fw blob + write_ram32
   (ramsize-4, 0) + resetcore INTERNAL_MEM + kimptoc's P1. READS stay:
   test.277 PRE-WRITE dump, 2 s poll, POST-POLL struct+HEAD -- si[+0x010]
   is published by the FW regardless of the host; when the fw does not
   publish (si[+0x010]=0), POST-POLL falls back to the Phase-4B-observed
   pointer 0x9af88 (test.317 branch) so the wr_idx discriminator survives
   without shared_info.

b) bcm4360_test317_no_olmsg: in brcmf_pcie_setup() skips the WHOLE
   post-release olmsg side -- select_core, request_irq (and the test.312b MBM
   RMW |=0x100), commonring hookup, brcmf_attach (preinit dcmds + the first
   H2D doorbell), test.312 gate, test.314 autopsies, fwcon timer -- and
   (with test309=1) enters bcm4360_t309_olmsg_zero_teardown_hold
   (MBM:=0, 10 s poll 1 Hz of the mailbox, SUMMARY; the device stays bound,
   no wiphy, no IRQ; reboot clears, do NOT rmmod). All evidence (poll end,
   POST-POLL struct/HEAD) is already on disk -- T276 2 s poll and T277
   POST-POLL run in brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram before this point.
   Console TAIL deliberately NOT ARMED (fire #10: full 25 dwords).

c) The test.276 poll gate (condition devinfo->t276_olmsg_buf) extended with
   bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo -- the poll READS si[+0x010]/fw_init_done/
   mbxint from the same addresses the fw fills anyway; with the value
   0x9af88 done. The change is exclusively in the gate condition, zero MMIO.

d) Independent parameters (like test.316_console_tail): they work on their
   own; no_sharedinfo requires test276=1/277=1 (evidence), no_olmsg requires
   test308=1+test309=1. Fire #11 discriminator:
   - console > 0x27d (1404 B + TRAP err 15 like at kimptoc) => our
     side-writes/bus master were the culprit (next bisect: side-writes OFF
     alone / no_master alone);
   - console == 0x27d => kimptoc's own 'release' (which did not clear the
     mailbox) and/or timing were to blame -- then R1: deep dive of the fw
     boot (SP/TCM dump via BAR2, breadcrumbs 0x62E20/0x18/0x88).

e) The fire #10 script updated for fire #11 (LOG_BASE test.317):
   bcm4360_test315=1 added (kimptoc P1 + no_master + discriminator),
   bcm4360_test315_no_master=1 (BM-off control), no_sharedinfo/no_olmsg
   =1; bcm4360_test316=1 stays (R3b -- test.28 substrate had no NVRAM);
   console_tail REMOVED. Setpci (ASPM off + CTO 10-100 ms) is applied by the
   main session before the fire, verified by readback.
diff --git i/brcmfmac/pcie.c w/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 41c9338..274a81c 100644
--- i/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ w/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -295,6 +295,13 @@ static uint bcm4360_test316_console_tail;
 module_param(bcm4360_test316_console_tail, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test316_console_tail, "BCM4360 test.316 console TAIL (INDEPENDENT of bcm4360_test316 -- runs whenever the test.277 POST-POLL console dump runs, i.e. with test277=1): after the existing first-128-B HEAD dump, read the LAST min(wr_idx, 96) bytes of the fw console buffer ending at wr_idx -- only the HEAD of the console is known so far and the last fw print before the stall is the key evidence (wr_idx=0x27d=637 in fires #6-#9). Same TCM dword-read mechanism as the HEAD dump (brcmf_pcie_read_ram32 into a stack chunk), read from the 4 B aligned start (<=3 B of earlier console text in front; the printed span ends exactly at wr_idx), printed as %*ph hex (<=64 B per line, one continuation line) + one %*pE ASCII-escaped line. Skipped with a log line when wr_idx=0 or the struct fails validation (buf_addr in TCM, wr_idx <= buf_size, test.278-style). (1=enable, 0=off)");
 
+static uint bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo;
+module_param(bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo, "BCM4360 test.317 fire #11 (maximal kimptoc test.28 replication, disc H3+H4): skip the WHOLE test.276 pre-release WRITE -- no dma_alloc of the 64 KB olmsg ring buffer, no ring-header memset/writes, no zeroing of the shared_info TCM region, no magic/dma_lo/dma_hi/buf_size/varsz/vars16/fw_init_done/magic_end writes (t276_olmsg_buf stays NULL and the 0016/0015/0014 post-release paths that need it are not reached -- no_olmsg skips them). The boot substrate becomes host-write-clean except: the fw blob copy, the core write_ram32(ramsize-4, 0), the INTERNAL_MEM resetcore, the test.315 P1 pre-release doorbell (kimptoc pcie_mask_irqs pattern) and the T309-hold MBM:=0 (post-evidence). READS stay: the test.277 PRE-WRITE dump, the 2 s poll, the POST-POLL struct + HEAD dump -- si[+0x010] is fw-published (the fw writes its own console ptr regardless of the host magic); when the fw skips publishing (si[+0x010]=0), the POST-POLL block falls back to the Phase-4B-observed 0x9af88 (test.317 branch) so the wr_idx discriminator survives. kimptoc test.28: no shared_info, no olmsg ring, BM-off -- his fw ran to 1404 B and TRAPped (err 15). (1=skip shared_info + ring writes, 0=default)");
+static uint bcm4360_test317_no_olmsg;
+module_param(bcm4360_test317_no_olmsg, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test317_no_olmsg, "BCM4360 test.317 fire #11: skip the ENTIRE olmsg post-release side -- select_core, request_irq (incl. the test.312b MBM RMW |=0x100), commonring hookup, brcmf_attach (preinit dcmds + the first H2D doorbell), the test.312 liveness gate, the test.314 autopsy, the fwcon timer: the host does ZERO writes after the ARM release + the test.315 discriminator reads. Instead: pr_emerg bracket + (if test309=1) bcm4360_t309_olmsg_zero_teardown_hold -- MBM:=0 (BAR0+0x4C, proven safe on fire #3) + 10 s 1 Hz mailbox poll + SUMMARY; the device stays bound, no wiphy, no IRQ armed, reboot clears, do NOT rmmod. The fire ends with evidence reads only (test.276 poll-end + test.277 POST-POLL struct/HEAD; console TAIL stays OFF -- the 25-dword burst killed printk in fire #10). Requires test308=1 + test309=1 (+ test276=1/test277=1 for the evidence); discriminator: console wr_idx > 0x27d (637) => side-writes/bus master were the culprit (fw goes to 1404 B + TRAP err 15 like kimptoc); == 0x27d => kimptoc's release/timing. (1=skip, 0=default)");
+
 static int bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc;
 module_param(bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc, "BCM4360 test.308: PCI-CDC (olmsg) transport, phase 1+2. Phase 1: replace the msgbuf sharedram-ptr handshake poll (TCM[ramsize-4], guaranteed -ENODEV on this fw) with a best-effort si[+0x2028] poll (10 ms x 200, then CONTINUE), skip msgbuf shared-struct/ring setup, proto_type=BCDC. Phase 2: txctl/rxctl over the olmsg ring (T276 DMA buffer -- requires bcm4360_test276_shared_info=1), D2H drain in the threaded ISR on BAR0+0x48 bit 8, per-cycle mask BAR0+0x4C |= 0x100. txdata stays a stub until phase 3. Gated: only for chip 4360; all other chips keep the msgbuf path. (1=enable, 0=off)");
@@ -3196,11 +3203,21 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 					 t277_struct[2], t277_struct[3]);
 			}
 
-			t276_buf = dma_alloc_coherent(&devinfo->pdev->dev,
-						      BCM4360_T276_OLMSG_BUF_SIZE,
-						      &t276_dma, GFP_KERNEL);
+			/* test.317: no_sharedinfo -- the host performs ZERO
+			 * pre-release writes into TCM/DMA (no ring buffer, no
+			 * shared_info): maximal kimptoc test.28 substrate. The
+			 * NULL t276_buf takes the !t276_buf branch below with
+			 * its own log line. */
+			t276_buf = NULL;
+			if (!bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo)
+				t276_buf = dma_alloc_coherent(&devinfo->pdev->dev,
+							      BCM4360_T276_OLMSG_BUF_SIZE,
+							      &t276_dma, GFP_KERNEL);
 			if (!t276_buf) {
-				pr_emerg("BCM4360 test.276: dma_alloc_coherent FAILED; skipping shared_info write\n");
+				if (bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo)
+					pr_emerg("BCM4360 test.317: shared_info + olmsg ring writes SKIPPED (no_sharedinfo=1 -- zero host TCM/DMA writes pre-release, kimptoc test.28 substrate; T276 poll + T277 POST-POLL dump below stay as READS on the fw-published si[+0x010])\n");
+				else
+					pr_emerg("BCM4360 test.276: dma_alloc_coherent FAILED; skipping shared_info write\n");
 			} else {
 				__le32 *p = (__le32 *)t276_buf;
 
@@ -3343,7 +3360,8 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 		 * response fields. Log on any change, continue for the
 		 * full 2 s (Phase 4B showed both TCM updates and mailbox
 		 * signals). */
-		if (bcm4360_test276_shared_info && devinfo->t276_olmsg_buf) {
+		if (bcm4360_test276_shared_info &&
+		    (devinfo->t276_olmsg_buf || bcm4360_test317_no_sharedinfo)) {
 			u32 last_fw_status = 0xdeadbeef;
 			u32 last_fw_init = 0xdeadbeef;
 			u32 last_mbxint = 0xdeadbeef;
@@ -3392,11 +3410,24 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 				pr_emerg("BCM4360 test.277: POST-POLL struct-ptr from si[+0x010]=0x%08x\n",
 					 t277_ptr);
 
+				/* test.317 fallback: on a no-write boot the fw may
+				 * skip publishing si[+0x010] -- fall back to the
